    <statement><p>State whether the equation</p>
<p><m>9 x^2 + 4 y^2 - 16 z^2=1</m></p>
<p>defines (enter number of statement):</p>
<p>1. A hyperboloid of two sheets</p>
<p>2. A hyperboloid of one sheet</p>
<p>3. An ellipsoid</p>
<p>4. None of these</p>
<p><fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\left( \frac{x}{\frac{1}{3}} \right)^2 + \left( \frac{y}{\frac{1}{2}} \right)^2 - \left( \frac{z}{\frac{1}{4}} \right)^2  =1</m> 



This equation is the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet. The correct answer is <m>2</m>.





</solution>
